[00:01:22.089] HIGHLIGHTS: There are two anomalies illustrated in this screenrecording; the first is the discrepancy between the signal strength icons at the opening scene, when the control center is shown as I began the capture; and the second is the example of notificaiton pops up that hackled me throughout my use of apps despite having disabled the notifications of the apps; the case illustrated by this screenrecording is the Journal app.

1) At the start of a screenrecording I observed a discrepancy between the signal strength show in the upper side status bar of the Control Center, and the signal strength shown inside the cell icon of the communications group widget (part of the main screen of the Control Center). The signal strength icon at the top-right of the Control Center, the icon to the left of the "Verizon 5GUW," showed three solid white bars. However, the cell icon shown inside the communications group widget, showed a signal strength pf only one bar solid white. Many of the captured screenrecording that begin with the Control Center as the opening scene, while I had the cellular service on, showed these two icons synchronized (i.e., the number of bars shown in the signal strength icon at the top of the interface, were reflected in the signal strength inside the bright green colored cell icon inside the communications group widget). To fully appreciate the discrepancy between these icons view screenrecording (a) and screenshot (b). Then to view the predominant appearance of the synchronized icons, view (this is not an exhaustive list) the opening scene of screenrecordings  (c), (e), and (g), the respective screenshots of these scenes are (d), (f), (h). Full filenames are listed below:   

